[Music]  as i started writing this volume i came  to recall what an old-fashioned chinese  man said about the white people  when asked if the white people were  civilized he made this categorical  statement  civilized far from it you can't civilize  these foreign devils  they are beyond redemption they live  weeks and months without touching a  mouthful of rice  but they eat the flesh of bullocks and  sheep in enormous quantities  nor do they eat meat cooked in small  pieces it is carried into the dining  room in huge chunks often half roar  they cut and slash and tear it apart and  they eat with knives and prongs  it makes a civilized being quite nervous  they even sit down with women around the  table  and the women are served first reversing  the order of nature  i could have written about the american  people in a similar vein in the first or  second week after my arrival in america  but now i cannot write in such a  superficial manner having spent a  quarter of a century as a lecturer in  various parts of the united states  i not only have observed but have  actually lived american life  at this critical hour in world history  when the earth is reverberating with all  sorts of false propaganda against  america  i felt it my duty as well as my  privilege to write a new volume  based on my more mature observation of  american life and culture  few asiatic authors have written about  america for their own people  who form nearly two-thirds of all human  beings  although i have not written this volume  exclusively for them i hope that it will  be read by many of my fellow asiatics  whose primary source of information  about america is the hostile  communist propaganda but will also help  my american friends  to gain a better understanding of their  own rich enviable heritage  [Music]  by and large a typical american is a  hard-working person  with boundless enthusiasm for work  he rises early in the morning often  startled out of bed by an alarm clock  he rushes to shave and dress but is  often held up by the terrific  task of mowing his barbed wire like  whiskers of which he is altogether too  much for he is about the hairiest man on  earth  coming closely behind the monkeys he now  grabs the shirt and swings it around him  and ties up his neck with a horrible  rope called necktie  as if he is going to hang himself he  then jumps into his trousers and his  shoes  too which was large as fair-sized canoes  for he has unusually big feet  he now races into the dining room and  gulps his breakfast door  often skips it and makes a beeline for  the garage bus or train  he finally reaches his office just about  half a second before the clock strikes  i think this application is filled out  all right mr arnold thank you  but once he starts his work and goes  about it as if he is going to pass out  at the end of the hour  but somehow he manages to survive  through the morning he rushes to the  lunchroom like a hungry tiger  he grabs a sandwich and throws the whole  business into his big mouth  he would have choked to death long ago  but for coffee which washes the sandwich  down to his tummy  he then runs back to his office and  works and works to him  work is his religion his recreation and  his life  you take work away from him and you will  kill him he is born to work he lives to  work and he dies  for his work he has no time to be  graceful polite and stylish  he rushes all the way from the maternity  ward to the graveyard  and at the graveyard he gets his first  real rest  in fact even after their death most  americans do not seem to get much rest  for some of them believe that heaven is  not a place of leisure but it is a sort  of  workshop where the souls of the mortal  beings play harps and sing and dance  with the angels  the bad americans however seem to get  some rest after their death  for according to some americans hell is  a place of rest  where there is nothing for a man to do  [Music]  this video is sponsored by magellan tv  the documentary streaming service  so quick update from coco she's cashed  in her bitcoin and sold her shares in  gamestop  and has pulled a controlling chair in  magellan tv so it's now called  coco tv i will have one documentary  constantly streaming of a bird  flying around in a circle i joke of  course magellan actually has more than 3  000 documentaries and new ones are  appearing all the time  a great example of this is our  recommendation this week ancient  angkor an exploration of the wonderful  temple complex  using the latest technology magellan is  essentially a netflix for documentaries  with the largest range of history stuff  anywhere amongst lots of other genres  much of it's available in 4k and  playable on a wide variety of devices  so click on the link in the description  for an exclusive month-long  free trial for voices of the past  viewers thanks  a typical american is a born optimist  he's not cast into gloom  by thousands of failures but he is  always exhilarated by one success  or a remote possibility of success which  may never come  the very belief that a man can shape his  own destiny was born of the american  experiences  in the new world of abundant  opportunities had the opportunities for  success been as scarce as in the old  world and  had americans suffered successive  defeats without end such as the people  of the old world  they too would probably have believed  that fate is what god or  nature decrees unfortunately these  sacred american ideals have not always  succeeded in penetrating the color line  for instance even at this moment when  the american boys are dying for freedom  in korea  the koreans japanese siamese indonesians  and polynesians are still excluded  from the citadel of american democracy  and those who are already in the united  states are not allowed to enjoy the  privilege of becoming  american citizens it is doubtful if  america can gain the wholehearted  support of the east for the cause of  freedom  without getting rid of this cancerous  disease  race prejudice  [Music]  despite this truly not until i found a  sanctuary in america did i have a taste  of liberty  having grown up under the shadows of the  japanese secret police and  manchurian bandits i did not know what  peace and freedom meant  i still remember how i felt when i had  the first taste of freedom in the sweet  land of liberty  out of the reach of japanese secret  police and chinese bandits  i'm putting it mildly when i say that my  first taste of freedom in america  was as thrilling as the first kiss of a  young lover  all the loose talk that there is no more  freedom in america than in the  totalitarian countries is outright  communist propaganda  or the foolish utterances of the  ignorant and irresponsible americans who  have enjoyed freedom and democracy for  so long  and so much in this blessed country that  they have forgotten the meaning  of tyranny and despotism even the rich  and powerful are often  sued defeated fined or jailed by the  common man  who was supposed to be a helpless slave  to his capitalist master  it is about the only great democratic  country in the world where any man  can criticize attack or condemn and  denounce his government  with no more compunction than he would  feel in scolding his dog  or in whipping his horse it is about the  only country under the sun where any man  can even call the president of his  country  s.o.b whatever that may mean and can  still retain his head  and go about the country as free as a  bird i think this fact  alone to call the president whatever one  wishes without fear  makes the united states the freest  country  in the world  traveling up and down the country i have  attacked and denounced the american  people and government for their  indifference with the pacific and far  eastern affairs  had i done this in a totalitarian state  i would have lost my head long ago  but no official or civilian has ever  questioned my right to say what i said  the only thing which have deprived me of  my freedom of speech and movement  have been the blizzards and the labor  strikes which stop the buses trains or  planes  the fine spirit of sportsmanship is  beautifully expressed  in almost every political election the  opposing candidates throw  mud at each other's faces and call each  other names in a way that no honorable  man would dream of doing  they shout yell and swear in the  strongest language as if they are going  to kill each other off  and get it over within a hurry certainly  few decent men on earth can think of  admiring a people who lie and cheat as  the american campaigners do  but the way they accept the result of  the election arouses the highest respect  of all men in most countries the loser  continues the battle after the election  he accuses the winner of using dishonest  methods in the election and refuses to  accept the result of the election  i'm not going to give in let us fight it  out so the election by ballots  ends in election by bullets but it is  not so  with americans both the winner and the  loser accept the election result as  final  although they know that the majority  cannot be right  always  americans waste little time on history  they study history only to find the  faults of their ancestors so that they  may not repeat the same mistakes  this forward-looking frame of mind as i  see it is one of the essential  differences between the occidental and  the oriental  particularly between the american and  the old chinese  the old-fashioned chinese revered their  ancestors so much as to worship them  and feared to do anything which their  ancestors did not do  on the other hand americans are never so  conservative or  so dogmatic as to scorn new ideas  though it is a fact that many of these  so-called new things are not really new  their modern music known as crooning  sounds little different  from the noise made by a sick dog hit by  a stone  their so-called modern art is a crude  and childish replica of the drawings of  the cavemen  with one difference the drawings of the  cavemen were intelligible whereas those  of the american modernists are not  the american women have not introduced  anything new when they wear trousers or  long fingernails the chinese women wore  trousers long before america was  discovered  one of the funniest new styles i've seen  in america was the so-called  cooly coat which at one time was worn by  almost every housewife who could afford  it  as i came to lecture at a fashionable  woman's club all the ladies came in  colorful  cooly coats bearing strange chinese  characters on their backs  one of them read i am a fire  extinguisher  another said i'm a water carrier still  another read  i'm a big fat fool  [Music]  even the poor americans accepting some  habitual drunkards or bums  can eat all the food which a man needs  and the rich men cannot possibly eat  more than the poor  the wives of the rich men are not better  fed than those of the poor men  for both classes of women just starved  to death not because they do not have  enough to eat but because they want to  be  fashionable in fact the only class of  underfed  undernourished and starving people i've  seen in all my 25 years of travelling in  america  is the class of women who voluntarily  subject themselves to starvation for the  sake of preserving  slender figures in old china only the  rich men and their wives and children  had enough to eat and to grow corpulent  corpulence therefore became a symbol of  fortune beauty and charm  one of the commonest flatteries was to  say to a person you look  fatter than before but here in america  everyone has more than enough to eat  and everyone can grow stout like the  millionaires in china  so corpulence is no sign of beauty or  honor  you call a lady a fat cow oh boy you are  sure to get into trouble  many american women grow so bony and  skinny that i feel sorry for the men  for it must be hard for them unless they  be archaeologists  to grow romantic with a bag of bones  [Music]  of all the things that make americans  happy and of all the things which make  them work like slaves in building their  civilization  the most important and the most powerful  is the thing  called love  it is no exaggeration to say that all  their struggle for success  wealth and honor has been motivated by  love  which has been glorified in legend and  fable in drama  music and literature so when i was a  student i fell for a beautiful  sweet little american co-ed i shall  never forget how i felt my eyes were  fixed on the stars my feet walked on the  drifting clouds  my heart was filled with something which  made me  sigh often my mind was blank and my head  swam about in a dreamland  i couldn't eat or sleep subsequently i  grew dizzy tired and weak and i felt as  if i caught a terrible flu  i did not know what it was at first when  i asked about it my american friends  told me that it was  love it was incredible and i asked  you mean to say this is the stuff which  you fight and die over  yep that's it said my friends well  i said if that is true i'm very sorry  for you people have nothing better to  fight for  personally i would rather catch another  [Music]  flu  modern americans born in a rich  prosperous country  with silver spoons in their mouths have  never seen  felt or understood the meaning of  poverty and misery  nor have they worked for or paid with  their own sweat blood and tears for what  they have  naturally they do not fully appreciate  what they have and are not content with  all the wealth and comfort found in  america whether happy or not  americans have built in their search for  happiness the mightiest material  civilization  known in history  what they have built has served both as  a target of attack  and an object of worship the critics of  american civilization usually say  in substance you have developed science  inventions but you have not  improved your men and women you have  built great homes  churches schools factories planes and  ships  but you have not developed your morals  and manners  you have leveled the mountains tamed the  rivers and transformed your deserts and  wildernesses into farms orchards and  parks  but you have not developed your cultural  and spiritual  qualities of life but in a way it is  fortunate for all democratic peoples  that america has put a priority on  developing her material power  had she been too much occupied with  producing her beethoven's miltons and  shakespeare's  to give thought to creating ford's  edisons and comptons  she might have gone down under the heels  of tojo or stalin  regardless of her beautiful art music  literature philosophy and religion  valuable though they are had she been  ruthlessly crushed as other countries  were  what nation would have served in her  place as an arsenal of democracy  and a reservoir of lifeblood for the  teeming millions  of the helpless and hopeless victims of  war  materialistic america i'd take my hat  off to thee  and i am once again

